4.Structured Concurrency (Incubator): Structured Concurrency allows multiple tasks to run concurrently in a structured scope where their lifecycle is managed together, improving reliability and error handling.
try (var scope = new StructuredTaskScope.ShutdownOnFailure()) { //This creates a task scope. Think of it like a task manager that controls multiple threads.
    Future<String> user = scope.fork(() -> fetchUser()); // task 1
    Future<Integer> order = scope.fork(() -> fetchOrder()); // task 2
    scope.join(); // This waits until all tasks finish. 
    scope.throwIfFailed(); // If one task fails, all other tasks stop automatically.

}
fork() starts tasks in parallel threads.
Main Thread
     │
     ▼
StructuredTaskScope
     │
     ├── Task 1 → fetchUser()
     │
     └── Task 2 → fetchOrder()

Both run in parallel

