9. Structured Concurrency (Preview)
try (var scope = new StructuredTaskScope.ShutdownOnFailure()) {
    Future<String> result1 = scope.fork(() -> task1());
    Future<String> result2 = scope.fork(() -> task2());
    scope.join().throwIfFailed();
}
-->Run task1 and task2 in parallel
-->Wait for them to finish
-->If any task fails → stop everything
Main Thread
     │
     ▼
StructuredTaskScope
     │
     ├── task1()
     └── task2()
Why This Feature Was Introduced
Before this feature developers used:
ExecutorService
CompletableFuture
manual thread management
Problems:
complex code
difficult error handling
thread leaks
Structured concurrency provides:
✔ cleaner code
✔ automatic cancellation
✔ safer lifecycle management
10.Key Encapsulation Mechanism API : KEM allows two parties to securely establish a shared secret key using public key cryptography, which can then be used for symmetric encryption.
KeyPairGenerator kpg = KeyPairGenerator.getInstance("X25519");
KeyPair kp = kpg.generateKeyPair();

Alice (Sender)  →  Bob (Receiver)
Bob → sends a LOCK (public key)
Alice → locks a box with that LOCK
Alice → sends locked box
Bob → opens it with his KEY (private key)

Why This Is Useful
This mechanism is used in modern secure systems like:
TLS 1.3
**Signal secure messaging
HTTPS encryption